"""
Flashback - AI Events Spine (FOUNDATIONAL PIPELINE, hardened) — v2.1 (per-account isolation)

This file is the canonical disk-backed event timeline used for learning correctness.

Core properties:
- Single-writer canonical outputs:
    Only THIS spine writes:
      state/ai_events/<ACCOUNT_LABEL>/setups.jsonl
      state/ai_events/<ACCOUNT_LABEL>/outcomes*.jsonl
      state/ai_events/<ACCOUNT_LABEL>/spine_events.jsonl
      state/ai_events/<ACCOUNT_LABEL>/pending_setups.json
      state/ai_memory/<ACCOUNT_LABEL>/*
- All producers emit to an inbox:
      state/ai_events_inbox_<ACCOUNT_LABEL>.jsonl   (main keeps legacy state/ai_events_inbox.jsonl)
  which the spine drains using a per-account cursor file.

Hardening:
- Strict JSONL discipline: if a target file exists and does not end with b"\n",
  inject a newline before appending the next line.
- Fail-soft: never crash callers.

Why this patch exists:
- Your system is multi-subaccount. A global spine output directory causes cross-account
  contamination and makes validation impossible.
"""

